# Untrace

One root install (`sudo python -m untrace --install --stealth-extension --launch-wrapper --chromedriver-cdc`) wires the Chrome launch wrapper, stealth extension, and chromedriver CDC patch. Re-run to update. Fix the wrapper, extension, and chromedriver — not the caller.

## Toolchain

- Use **uv** only (`uv sync --group dev`, `uv run …`). Do not reintroduce Poetry. Task runners: `uv run task <name>` (taskipy in the dev group).
- Lint: `uv run task lint` / `uv run task lint-check`
- Unit tests: `uv run task test`
- Browser tests: `uv run task test-browser` (requires a prior full install)

## Install / uninstall

- Feature flags are independent: `--stealth-extension`, `--launch-wrapper` (Chrome launch wrapper + random profiles), `--chromedriver-cdc`. Bare `--install` enables all.
- **`sudo --uninstall` must remove everything** — system Chrome wrapper (`chrome_real` restore), `/etc/untrace`, **and** user tree at `~/.local/share/untrace` for `SUDO_USER` (not just `/root`). Unpatch chromedrivers. Never leave user tree behind with a “not removed” note.
- Commands under `sudo` / `pkexec` must resolve the real user’s home via `linux_invoking_pw()` (`SUDO_USER` / `PKEXEC_UID`) and `home_dirs_to_search()` — not `Path.home()` as root alone. Chromedriver/selenium caches live under the invoker’s `~/.cache`.
- Install/uninstall entrypoints elevate via `ensure_privileges()` (pkexec/sudo / UAC). Do not leave sticky `use_untrace_root()` overrides after install/uninstall.

## Windows

- **Stealth** uses Chrome Web Store force-install (`ExtensionInstallForcelist` + External Extensions `update_url`), not the Linux local pack/seed path. Warm `%PROGRAMDATA%\Untrace\chrome_profile_template` once (Chrome writes `Secure Preferences` `location: 7`), then copy into each `--user-data-dir`. Preference seeding cannot fake Secure Preferences. Non-enterprise Chrome blocks local/`http://` force-install hosts. Do **not** use localhost update XML, `file://` CRX, or `--load-extension`. Do not revive deleted Linux policy/CRX or Windows local-update/seed writers without an explicit product decision.
- **Never strip or blank `--enable-automation`** (wrapper or chromedriver). Chrome exits under `--remote-debugging-port` without it. Chromedriver patch: CDC + blank `test-type=webdriver` only. SAC/WDAC may block the unsigned PE (`WinError 4551`) — warn in README/CLI. Selenium-manager remains Linux-only.
- **C# wrapper:** detect automation, strip chromedriver junk (except `--enable-automation`), apply launcher flags, `WaitForExit`, Job Object `KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE`. Manual and Selenium use `%TEMP%\chrome_random_profiles\profile_*`; Selenium `scoped_dir` is a junction into that tree.
- Guard Unix-only APIs (`pwd`, `geteuid`, Unix paths). Deploy roots: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Untrace` / `%PROGRAMDATA%\Untrace`.

## No workarounds

- Do **not** split behavior beyond documented platform constraints (e.g. stealth only for Selenium, flags-only for manual, separate code paths “because manual is different”).
- Do **not** punt with excuses (“Akamai is intermittent”, “can’t fix without test options”) when a test fails — keep fixing untrace until it passes.
- Do **not** add test-side Chrome flags/options, or one-off CLI band-aids, instead of fixing install/wrapper/extension.

## Browser integration tests (`tests/test_chromedriver.py`)

- **`chrome_driver` is hands-off.** `tests/conftest.py` stays minimal: `webdriver.Chrome(options=Options())`, yield, quit. The only allowed toggle is the `HEADLESS` module variable (`False` by default; when `True`, pass `--headless=new`). Do **not** add anything else unless the user explicitly asks — no pytest CLI options, env/`PATH` hacks, extra Chrome args, custom capabilities, service config, retries, screenshots, or logging.
- If a bot test fails, fix untrace (wrapper → CDC patch → extension) — **not** `chrome_driver` or the test file. Stealth/flags/CDC come from the installed stack.
- Run: `uv run pytest tests/test_chromedriver.py` (requires a prior `--install --stealth-extension --launch-wrapper --chromedriver-cdc`).
- **Never auto-run `--install` from tests** — user controls install state; tests must not mutate it.
- **Akamai blocks are detection failures**, not “wait and retry.” “Access Denied” / “Something went wrong” on `test_bot_akamai` (e.g. hilton.com) means untrace is leaking — fix until it passes. Use `WebDriverWait` (30s max) for readiness — no fixed `time.sleep` polling.

## Code quality

- **No unnecessary comments.** Comment only when logic is non-obvious or a constraint must be preserved.
- **No unnecessary tests.** Every test must protect real behavior the user cares about.
- **No dead imports or symbols.** Before finishing a change, remove unused imports, variables, and helpers from every file you touched.
- Shared path/home/chown/assets helpers live in `untrace/paths.py` — do not re-duplicate them across modules. Prefer `IS_WINDOWS` from there over scattered `sys.platform` checks.
- Prefer **pathlib** (`Path`) over `os.path` / bare `open` / `os.chmod` / `os.makedirs`. Ruff enforces `UP` + `PTH`.
